WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:02.469
(cars passing)

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:04.020
- [Interviewer] All right, Angel.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:04.960
- Yes.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:05.827
- [Interviewer] Angel,
where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.827 --> 00:00:07.940
Where are you from, originally?

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.763
- Originally from the Harbor
area, San Pedro, California.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.060
I was born in Torrance,

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.640
raised in San Pedro

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.650
and some of here and there.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.440
- [Interviewer] And you grew
up with both your parents?

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.033
- No, actually, I didn't.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:28.560
My mom and my dad
separated when I was young

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.010
and it was, I don't know the reasons

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.040
that they did separate.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.740
Up to this day I still don't know.

00:00:36.037 --> 00:00:37.024
But I do know that maybe

00:00:37.024 --> 00:00:41.500
around two years old, I was, I guess,

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.820
my dad had took me from my mom,

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:45.880
and somehow we ended up

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.433
in San Jose, California.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:51.580
By the time my mom got me back,

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.140
mind you, I was a toddler,

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.100
I was only two years old,

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.270
I had a third-degree burn

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:58.880
on the top of my head.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.100
And the story was that,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.420
up to this day that I
still, you know, hear is

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:06.840
that I had grabbed a pot from the stove,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.730
but I'm two years old,

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.580
how can I reach the stove?

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.030
And I still have the scar

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:11.970
on the top of my head,

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.840
but it's shrank throughout the years.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.320
I'm 52 years old now,

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.080
so 50 years ago,

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.517
but it's still, the scar's still there.

00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:19.620
But it scarred me.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.100
It scarred me from that day,

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.250
because I've always
had a complex about it.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.330
Like I said, I don't know
what really happened.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:28.230
My mom don't know.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.350
We really don't know what happened.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.360
But my mom got me back.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.353
They separated some time after that.

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.807
And then my mom remarried again.

00:01:37.807 --> 00:01:38.850
(puppy yawns)

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:42.883
And that was another story that, you know,

00:01:44.925 --> 00:01:46.045
it wasn't nothing happy,

00:01:46.045 --> 00:01:48.980
nothing that I've ever, you know,

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:52.070
I could even think of
has been a happy part

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.740
in my entire life.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:55.830
But you learn to deal

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.640
with situations in your life

00:01:58.640 --> 00:01:59.700
and either accept it

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.590
or, you know, you can try to change it.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.033
And I've tried to do both.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:07.970
Eventually I started growing up.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:12.233
I was 17, 16, 17 when I left home.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.290
I left home by myself,

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:18.300
came out to the LA area

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.550
and I went from one crowd to another.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:23.900
I've been transgender
since I've been like, 13.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.790
And they, I think, you know,
they've always known it,

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:29.030
so that even made it double harder on me.

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:33.640
They, all my family are gang members

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:36.610
from my mom to my dad.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:38.670
So all my uncles, they're all gang members

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:39.763
from the Harbor area.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.670
So that was double rough on me.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:45.363
So I've grown up around a lot of violence.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.150
And like I said, you know,

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.050
I've always tried to make

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.500
even a good situation out of a bad one,

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.070
but somehow, you know, I wasn't just,

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.790
I didn't have that luck.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:55.880
So I did leave home.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:59.110
I left home and I just
tried to change, you know,

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.890
something that I felt

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:03.020
that maybe it could be better for me

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:04.620
if I separated from all of them.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.120
It wasn't all good.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.380
You know, I have moments

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.987
that I can say that, you know,

00:03:10.987 --> 00:03:12.520
"Okay, well, this wasn't too bad."

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.770
But who's to say

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.270
that it's not too bad for one person

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.720
when it could be for another?

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.520
- [Interviewer] Is there,
was there child abuse?

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:21.357
- Oh yeah there was, big time.

00:03:21.357 --> 00:03:23.100
- What--
- My stepfather.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.010
When my mom had remarried,

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:27.780
that's one of the reasons I had left home.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.150
When my mom had been married

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.740
and she ended up having my sister first,

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:34.030
and she, her name was Monique.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:34.870
Then she turned around

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.620
and she had my brother, Jacob.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:37.720
And there abuse

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.810
throughout the whole,
their whole relationship.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.853
And it was always focused on me.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:44.273
I have a older brother.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:46.335
My mom would always take him,

00:03:46.335 --> 00:03:49.170
and somehow I held her
accountable for that,

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.180
because I felt like, you know,

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:51.470
maybe she knew what was going on

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:52.610
because of the situation

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:54.450
with, you know, my sexuality.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.970
They all knew what was gonna happen.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:57.893
You know, I didn't understand it.

00:03:57.893 --> 00:03:58.740
I was young.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.220
I was too young.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:01.860
To me, I've always been a girl,

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.453
but, you know, when you have
somebody keep pounding it

00:04:03.453 --> 00:04:06.260
into you, you know, "You're
a boy, you're a boy,"

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.483
you, it becomes a problem, mentally.

00:04:09.547 --> 00:04:12.140
So from one day to another,

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.860
I would have my clothes taken from me,

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:14.790
thrown in the trash,

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.490
because they didn't like the
clothes that I was wearing.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.323
Could I let her down?

00:04:18.323 --> 00:04:19.530
- [Interviewer] Yeah, please.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.020
- I would, you know, find
my stuff in the trash

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:22.903
and I would go take it out.

00:04:25.015 --> 00:04:26.560
I'd go take it out of the trash

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:27.620
and I'd, you know, put it back.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:28.959
- Where'd you put it?
- I'd put it back

00:04:28.959 --> 00:04:30.750
and she would turn around

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.297
and my mom would tell me,

00:04:32.297 --> 00:04:33.397
"You can't be acting up.

00:04:33.397 --> 00:04:34.470
"You're gonna get in trouble."

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:38.140
I remember one time I had turned around

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:39.840
and I had these pair of shorts.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.123
I was 12 years old,

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:44.200
and I'll never forget that.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.470
You know, to me, I've
always been, like I said,

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.410
I believed that I was a girl.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:50.880
So anytime that they seen

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.770
that I was doing something
out of my character

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:56.020
that they felt that
wasn't, you know, boyish,

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.400
I would get punished for it.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.040
It went from standing in the corner

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:02.810
for 15 minutes, maybe to an hour,

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:04.770
and the more that I rebelled

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.160
and I didn't go along with

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.300
what they wanted me to do,

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.610
the longer I was in there.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:10.393
Then it went from that to physical.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.120
And my mom always act
like she didn't know,

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:13.953
but she knew.

00:05:13.953 --> 00:05:15.410
She knew it was went on.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.910
And you know, I went from that

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.790
to just arguments between them

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:23.670
because of me, because
I wouldn't, you know,

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:24.740
keep my mouth shut.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.243
And I wouldn't, you know, do the things

00:05:26.243 --> 00:05:27.520
that they wanted me to do.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:28.880
And I never wanted my hair cut

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:30.010
because of that burn that I had

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.954
on the top of my head.

00:05:31.954 --> 00:05:35.020
When they turned around
and they told me that they

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.050
were gonna cut my hair off intentionally,

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.880
I ran away from home for the first time.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:41.100
When I ran away from home,

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.233
I was gone for two weeks the first time.

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:47.610
The second time I left home was

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.140
about three weeks to a month,

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:50.000
and they found me.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.140
My stepdad, I don't know how he found me,

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:56.080
but he went to my friend's
house where I was at.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.880
He kicked the door in.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.550
He went straight through the
whole house looking for me.

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:01.590
He found me in the kitchen.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.420
He grabbed me by my throat.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.893
He slammed me up against the refrigerator,

00:06:08.006 --> 00:06:09.410
(Angel sighs)

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:13.163
and I'm 12, I don't know the difference.

00:06:15.703 --> 00:06:17.870
I don't know, you know, what I did wrong.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.120
All I know is that I
didn't want to be there.

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:27.050
I tried to accept things, you know,

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:28.480
for what they are.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.080
Some things you could change,
some things you can't.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:35.630
But he took me home with him

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:37.990
and my mom and him argued
for a couple of days.

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:39.650
They went, kept going on and on and on,

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:42.607
and I told her every time I had
a chance, I was gonna leave,

00:06:42.607 --> 00:06:44.183
and I wasn't gonna come back.

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:48.053
So finally, I don't know what my mom,

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:49.963
I don't know what was going

00:06:49.963 --> 00:06:51.390
through my mom's head at that time,

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:54.063
but I know it was affecting her too.

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:59.370
And I remember her, she
had a little .22 or .25 gun

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:00.330
that she kept in her drawer.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:03.530
And I remembered I didn't
go to school that day.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:05.920
And I seen her chasing
him down the stairs.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:08.450
We lived in these
apartments in Montebello.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:11.863
And she chased him down the
street, shooting the gun,

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.660
and she called my uncles to come get us.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.720
And they came and got us,

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.120
and we never went back
to Montebello after that.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:21.569
- [Interviewer] So did you suspect

00:07:21.569 --> 00:07:23.633
there might have been
sexual abuse at some point?

00:07:23.633 --> 00:07:26.405
- With my father, I don't, I'm not sure.

00:07:26.405 --> 00:07:27.295
I don't know, like I said,

00:07:27.295 --> 00:07:29.334
I don't know what really happened.

00:07:29.334 --> 00:07:31.330
I don't know why, you
know, he did the things

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.250
that he did to me.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:35.160
I don't know why him and my mom separated

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:35.993
from the beginning.

00:07:35.993 --> 00:07:37.220
I don't know why he took me

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.210
and he didn't take my
other, my older brother,

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:40.930
because I don't look nothing like him.

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.420
I don't look nothing like my mother,

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:43.390
a little bit like my mother,

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:44.900
but not too much.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.560
My father, I don't look nothing like him,

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:49.110
but I looked like his sister a little bit.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.523
I resemble her a little bit.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:55.270
Like I said, I've always, you know,

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:59.220
there's always those
you-want-to-know's, you know?

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:02.320
Could it have, could it not have?

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:03.153
Why, why me?

00:08:03.153 --> 00:08:04.440
You know, I've been through a lot,

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:05.760
like I said, throughout the years,

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.510
and it's always been something tragic

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:09.240
or it always been something

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:11.970
that, you know, weren't good memories.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.530
And I still have those.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:15.770
So when I finally left home at 16,

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:17.030
after all that happened, you know,

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:18.410
I felt, you know, maybe

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:20.590
if I just go somewhere on my own

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:23.590
that I could start fresh

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:24.480
where nobody knew me.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.500
I could just, you know, be me.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:29.690
I wouldn't have to, you
know, try to, you know,

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:30.670
hide who I was,

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:32.040
even though I wasn't hiding nothing.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.020
I was me, really.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:35.310
You know, I just, I didn't care.

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:36.830
I didn't care what anybody said.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:39.800
You know, I've always felt,

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:42.470
if I can't be myself and
accept me for who I am,

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:44.283
how's anybody else gonna accept me?

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:47.100
But still, I went through a lot of issues,

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.540
a lot of trials and tribulations.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.260
I went through a lot of hard times,

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:51.200
a lot of hard times.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:52.090
And even though, you know,

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.900
I tried to make things work

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:55.650
that didn't work for me either way.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.030
At 16, when I left home,

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:01.303
I came back towards the LA area,

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:04.430
and I stood out here.

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:05.690
I lived in Monterey park

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:07.389
for like maybe a year or so

00:09:07.389 --> 00:09:08.610
with some of my friends that I had

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:09.903
from when I was younger.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:13.913
And then I started getting into trouble.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:17.170
Money was never easy.

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:19.440
You know, I've never really had a real job

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:21.010
except for maybe two of them

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:22.593
that they got rid of me

00:09:22.593 --> 00:09:24.200
because I lied about my age.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.593
I was under age, so they had to let me go.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:28.980
So I went from one thing to another,

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:31.183
then prostitution came in.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:33.560
It seemed like it was easy money.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:34.430
That's always something

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:36.200
that they've, you know,

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.500
that not all people,

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.910
but there's a I can say at least 85%

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:42.730
of the guys that I meet,

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:45.780
it always has something to
do with something sexual.

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:48.540
And I've learned to come to accept that.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:52.034
You know, either I accept it or, you know,

00:09:52.034 --> 00:09:54.080
I'm just gonna be miserable my whole life,

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.950
so I've learned to adapt

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:59.560
and work with who and what I am.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:02.010
There's, you know, there's
no easy way to say it.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:06.650
So I started working the streets.

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:09.883
I started out in El Monte first.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:12.380
Then it went from that

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:16.260
to doing federal crimes,

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.870
cashing checks and whatnot.

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:21.110
And in the process of me doing that,

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:26.293
I ended up getting into a lot
of altercations on the streets

00:10:26.293 --> 00:10:27.662
with different individuals

00:10:27.662 --> 00:10:28.900
and it became cases.

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:31.773
But I wasn't the one that,

00:10:31.773 --> 00:10:33.590
I wasn't the person that had started it

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:35.520
or I wasn't the aggressor, you know,

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.963
I've always felt that I needed to,

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:41.170
I needed to protect myself

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:42.710
because if I didn't protect myself,

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:44.800
