00:40:18.395 --> 00:40:19.730
It's not even myself.

00:40:19.730 --> 00:40:22.840
I care more for them
than I care for myself.

00:40:22.840 --> 00:40:23.910
And you know, that's sad,

00:40:23.910 --> 00:40:26.610
but at the same time, you
know, they mean a lot to me.

00:40:28.120 --> 00:40:31.170
But like I said, I've learned to adapt

00:40:31.170 --> 00:40:35.063
and I've learned to put a mask on.

00:40:36.240 --> 00:40:37.700
I do it for my own protection,

00:40:37.700 --> 00:40:39.100
because if I don't,

00:40:39.100 --> 00:40:41.420
people will see what I've been through

00:40:41.420 --> 00:40:43.210
or they'll see, you know,

00:40:43.210 --> 00:40:44.700
how vulnerable that I can be.

00:40:44.700 --> 00:40:45.930
And I am very vulnerable.

00:40:45.930 --> 00:40:48.580
I can say it, honestly say that I am.

00:40:48.580 --> 00:40:50.527
But I've learned to put that mask on.

00:40:50.527 --> 00:40:52.400
And it makes me feel safer,

00:40:52.400 --> 00:40:53.880
because if I don't put that mask on.

00:40:53.880 --> 00:40:56.890
I feel like, you know,
the worst can happen.

00:40:56.890 --> 00:40:58.543
And if, it's not me, you
know, dying or anything.

00:40:58.543 --> 00:41:00.140
That's not the worst.

00:41:00.140 --> 00:41:01.950
It's them, you know, my dogs.

00:41:01.950 --> 00:41:02.860
What's gonna happen to them

00:41:02.860 --> 00:41:03.720
if something happens to me?

00:41:03.720 --> 00:41:04.560
Nobody's gonna take care

00:41:04.560 --> 00:41:06.110
of them like I do, nobody will.

00:41:07.880 --> 00:41:09.143
So I wear that mask.

00:41:09.143 --> 00:41:11.000
I walk around here with that fake smile

00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:13.390
and, you know, like everything's
okay, but it's not okay.

00:41:13.390 --> 00:41:14.223
It's not okay.

00:41:14.223 --> 00:41:15.470
And it never will be okay.

00:41:15.470 --> 00:41:17.910
I'll never be able to
recapture those years

00:41:17.910 --> 00:41:20.490
that I lost, you know,
of any good memories

00:41:20.490 --> 00:41:21.590
or of my childhood

00:41:21.590 --> 00:41:22.960
where I could say I had a happy childhood.

00:41:22.960 --> 00:41:23.987
No, I never had a happy childhood.

00:41:23.987 --> 00:41:27.000
I don't know how to express

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:28.360
who I really am, you know,

00:41:28.360 --> 00:41:30.330
without having some part

00:41:30.330 --> 00:41:32.500
of my past come and hit me in the head.

00:41:32.500 --> 00:41:35.200
Because I know what I've
been through, I know.

00:41:35.200 --> 00:41:36.033
These people don't,

00:41:36.033 --> 00:41:38.360
none of these people really
know what happens to me

00:41:38.360 --> 00:41:39.330
or what happened to me

00:41:39.330 --> 00:41:40.480
or what will happen to me

00:41:40.480 --> 00:41:42.640
if I just let that mask off.

00:41:42.640 --> 00:41:44.060
They don't know.

00:41:44.060 --> 00:41:44.960
They don't know.

00:41:44.960 --> 00:41:46.590
But I've learned, like I said, to adapt.

00:41:46.590 --> 00:41:49.200
I adapt to situations as they come.

00:41:49.200 --> 00:41:51.690
Because if I plan anything beforehand,

00:41:51.690 --> 00:41:54.180
it won't turn out the way
that I want it, it won't.

00:41:54.180 --> 00:41:55.813
Something, and walk up or something,

00:41:55.813 --> 00:41:58.670
There's so many people that talk to me

00:41:58.670 --> 00:42:00.670
out here that know me.

00:42:00.670 --> 00:42:01.503
But don't think they just,

00:42:01.503 --> 00:42:03.170
because, oh, I'm a good person, no.

00:42:03.170 --> 00:42:04.290
They've all tried to hit on me.

00:42:04.290 --> 00:42:05.540
The ones that have, you know,

00:42:05.540 --> 00:42:07.390
even people that trying to introduce me

00:42:07.390 --> 00:42:09.560
to, you know, you, I guess,

00:42:09.560 --> 00:42:10.890
at one time or another.

00:42:10.890 --> 00:42:12.340
They've hit on me too.

00:42:12.340 --> 00:42:14.183
But I've learned how to just smile it off

00:42:14.183 --> 00:42:17.303
and, you know, push them
off little by little.

00:42:17.303 --> 00:42:20.090
But you know, with sarcasm

00:42:20.090 --> 00:42:21.150
or something, you know, smart.

00:42:21.150 --> 00:42:23.250
Just say, "Oh, I'm busy,"
or something like that

00:42:23.250 --> 00:42:24.600
instead of opening that door.

00:42:24.600 --> 00:42:27.380
Because I know once that door
is open, I'm gonna lose it.

00:42:27.380 --> 00:42:28.840
I will lose it, I will.

00:42:28.840 --> 00:42:31.130
And it's not that I'm a real tough person,

00:42:31.130 --> 00:42:32.480
'cause I'm not, I'm fragile.

00:42:32.480 --> 00:42:34.500
And I know I'm fragile to a certain degree

00:42:34.500 --> 00:42:36.790
until I feel like I'm
trapped into a corner.

00:42:36.790 --> 00:42:38.010
Once I'm trapped into a corner,

00:42:38.010 --> 00:42:42.500
I don't think about anything
else but, you know, my safety.

00:42:42.500 --> 00:42:43.910
It's either me or them,

00:42:43.910 --> 00:42:46.250
and it's not even prison
that worries me anymore,

00:42:46.250 --> 00:42:47.270
because it's not that.

00:42:47.270 --> 00:42:50.120
It's just, I am tired of
people taking advantage of me.

00:42:50.120 --> 00:42:50.953
I'm tired of it.

00:42:50.953 --> 00:42:53.480
I'm tired of people
using me for, you know,

00:42:53.480 --> 00:42:54.640
their own disposal.

00:42:54.640 --> 00:42:57.030
And they don't have any kind of caring

00:42:57.030 --> 00:42:58.880
or remorse in their heart.

00:42:58.880 --> 00:42:59.713
They don't care.

00:42:59.713 --> 00:43:02.690
They don't care, they don't
care about the next person.

00:43:02.690 --> 00:43:04.750
And I'm just the opposite.

00:43:04.750 --> 00:43:06.010
I'm opposite than all that.

00:43:06.010 --> 00:43:07.780
I help people when I can help them.

00:43:07.780 --> 00:43:08.880
And it's not because, you know,

00:43:08.880 --> 00:43:10.600
I'm easily influenced

00:43:10.600 --> 00:43:11.970
or, you know, I'm a pushover.

00:43:11.970 --> 00:43:12.880
It's not because of that.

00:43:12.880 --> 00:43:15.080
It's because even though I have been

00:43:15.080 --> 00:43:16.810
through everything that I have,

00:43:16.810 --> 00:43:19.913
I haven't lost being human.

00:43:22.340 --> 00:43:25.000
I haven't lost, you know, the ability

00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:27.290
to try to help somebody that I see

00:43:27.290 --> 00:43:28.573
that, you know, needs it.

00:43:29.950 --> 00:43:31.689
And I won't let that, I won't let that,

00:43:31.689 --> 00:43:34.000
I won't let that take take over me.

00:43:34.000 --> 00:43:36.260
These people that are
down here, the majority

00:43:36.260 --> 00:43:37.970
of them are down here

00:43:37.970 --> 00:43:40.010
and they got trapped down here

00:43:40.010 --> 00:43:42.050
And they don't know, they
don't know nothing better

00:43:42.050 --> 00:43:43.320
than to take advantage of people

00:43:43.320 --> 00:43:45.350
or try to get over on somebody.

00:43:45.350 --> 00:43:48.000
And I told myself, I would
never let that happen.

00:43:48.000 --> 00:43:49.570
I will never change like that.

00:43:49.570 --> 00:43:51.920
Because that's not who I am.

00:43:51.920 --> 00:43:53.140
I've had it happen to me.

00:43:53.140 --> 00:43:54.116
I've had all the worst

00:43:54.116 --> 00:43:56.120
that anybody can imagine happen to them.

00:43:56.120 --> 00:43:57.990
It's happened to me.

00:43:57.990 --> 00:43:59.870
It's happened to me, but I'm here.

00:43:59.870 --> 00:44:01.520
I'm a survivor.

00:44:01.520 --> 00:44:02.580
I'm a survivor,

00:44:02.580 --> 00:44:04.730
and if it wasn't for,

00:44:04.730 --> 00:44:05.750
I'm not gonna say the three of them,

00:44:05.750 --> 00:44:06.590
'cause I just got her.

00:44:06.590 --> 00:44:09.330
If it wasn't for my first one, Chloe,

00:44:09.330 --> 00:44:10.960
I wouldn't be here now.

00:44:10.960 --> 00:44:15.700
She has kept me from
day one from blowing up.

00:44:15.700 --> 00:44:18.600
She has kept me from going back to prison

00:44:18.600 --> 00:44:21.627
and she has given me the
will to want to be here

00:44:21.627 --> 00:44:23.053
and to take care of her.

00:44:24.010 --> 00:44:26.720
If I don't take care of her, nobody will.

00:44:26.720 --> 00:44:28.760
And she'll just be
another statistic out here

00:44:28.760 --> 00:44:32.380
just using her just to get
pregnant to sell her puppies.

00:44:32.380 --> 00:44:35.070
And you know, I'm not gonna
let that happen to her.

00:44:35.070 --> 00:44:38.400
I'm not gonna let nobody
use her like I've been used.

00:44:38.400 --> 00:44:39.410
And I've been used.

00:44:39.410 --> 00:44:41.870
I've been used over and over
and over and over again.

00:44:41.870 --> 00:44:43.470
And I've accepted it every time,

00:44:43.470 --> 00:44:44.970
until I just can't take it no more.

00:44:44.970 --> 00:44:47.690
And I just, you know, push people away.

00:44:47.690 --> 00:44:49.330
So that's what I do.

00:44:49.330 --> 00:44:51.870
That's me, I push people
away to a certain point,

00:44:51.870 --> 00:44:54.320
but I can communicate with people

00:44:54.320 --> 00:44:57.540
at a, you know, the same level
as they communicate with me,

00:44:57.540 --> 00:44:59.170
but I'm not a happy person

00:44:59.170 --> 00:45:01.990
and I don't feel safe
around people, I don't.

00:45:01.990 --> 00:45:03.320
I have to be by myself

00:45:03.320 --> 00:45:06.320
with my dogs to feel
really safe to a degree,

00:45:06.320 --> 00:45:07.990
because I'm always thinking
somebody's gonna try

00:45:07.990 --> 00:45:09.110
to do something.

00:45:09.110 --> 00:45:11.060
So here we are now.

00:45:11.060 --> 00:45:14.190
And you know, I'm 52 years old now,

00:45:14.190 --> 00:45:17.830
and my lifestyle has
changed to a certain degree.

00:45:17.830 --> 00:45:22.010
But I still can say I'm a survivor.

00:45:22.010 --> 00:45:24.550
I'm not one of the people
that have fell down

00:45:24.550 --> 00:45:27.540
and continue to where I'll
just disappear into the cracks.

00:45:27.540 --> 00:45:29.690
I'm not gonna let that happen.

00:45:29.690 --> 00:45:31.810
You can do it if you want to, you can.

00:45:31.810 --> 00:45:33.400
You can survive.

00:45:33.400 --> 00:45:35.350
You can even be on
drugs but still survive,

00:45:35.350 --> 00:45:36.770
because you have to have
some kind of humanity.

00:45:36.770 --> 00:45:38.510
You have to care about yourself

00:45:38.510 --> 00:45:39.520
to a certain degree

00:45:39.520 --> 00:45:41.730
for you to push it away little by little.

00:45:41.730 --> 00:45:44.100
But nobody knows what everybody
else goes through down here.

00:45:44.100 --> 00:45:45.387
You don't, you don't know.

00:45:45.387 --> 00:45:46.713
You don't know.

00:45:47.680 --> 00:45:49.060
The one thing I can say is

00:45:49.060 --> 00:45:51.150
that I am me and I always will be me

00:45:51.150 --> 00:45:51.983
no matter what.

00:45:51.983 --> 00:45:54.410
I've been through the worst that can be.

00:45:54.410 --> 00:45:55.940
But I'm still here.

00:45:55.940 --> 00:45:56.963
I'm still here.

00:45:58.930 --> 00:46:00.400
Yep, that's my story.

00:46:00.400 --> 00:46:01.402
- [Interviewer] Thank you
so much for talking to me.

00:46:01.402 --> 00:46:02.252
- You're welcome.

00:46:03.404 --> 00:46:05.071
You're very welcome.

00:46:06.131 --> 00:46:07.298
Come on, Nana.

